{t: Play That Funky Music}
{st: Wild Cherry}
{key: E}
{tempo: 108}

{sot: Intro}
| E7          | E7          | E7          | E7          |
{eot}

{sot: Verse}
| E7          | E7          | E7          | E7          |
| E7          | E7          | E7          | E7          |
{eot}

{sot: Chorus}
| A7          | A7          | E7          | E7          |
| B7          | A7          | E7          | E7          |
{eot}

{sot: Solo}
| E7          | E7          | E7          | E7          |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
70s Funk Rock Anthem: Built around a driving, high-energy 16th-note rhythm groove
in E Mixolydian / E Blues.

Rhythm Guitar: Keep the right hand locked into a continuous 16th-note scratch
pattern. Use tight, percussive E9 shell voicings on the top strings, emphasizing
the upbeat stabs.

Chorus Dynamics: The chorus shifts from the static E7 funk vamp into a classic
blues-rock turnaround moving through A7 and B7 before dropping back into the root.

Lead & Horns: Crisp trumpet and sax lines double the vocal melodies and punctuate
the breaks between the verse lines.
{eov}